      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Soo Line Railroad shipped everything from cream to cattle out of McLeod.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://ransomcountynd.net/mcleod/",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "McLeod is the only village in the 300 square mile Sandhill area of Sheyenne National Grasslands.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://ransomcountynd.net/mcleod/",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The drought of the 1930s devastated its trade area; fields became dunes of sand, pastures eroded, and groves of trees were buried.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://ransomcountynd.net/mcleod/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "McLeod Museum, built in 1909 on First Street, houses the Presbyterian Church and the historical preservation society’s artifacts.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://ransomcountynd.net/mcleod/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "McLeod School operated from 1907 to 2002 and now serves as a community event space with a kitchen and dining room for up to 80 people.",
